direction: down
goal: "Gambit modernization target\nMore capability + explicit semantics/resources + sustainable evolution\nPreserve Scheme strengths; retire obsolete hidden policy owners\nOCaml lessons are cross-layer design constraints, not a feature score"
semantic: "Language / compiler authority\nScheme semantics, G3 completion, root/control identity\nNegotiated HostGraph / FrameSpec / native profiles\nHigher-order and continuation optimization have their own gates"
runtime: "Runtime modernization\nVM / processor participation and memory ordering\nGC roots / barriers / callbacks / blocking / capture\nExisting Gambit machinery retained and explicitly refined"
njs: "NJS engineering boundary\nOne reaper owner; bounded query bytes\nIndependent termination / EOF / close / delivery states\nStructured failures, versioned inputs and conditional retirement"
providers: "Replaceable native engineering\nModern C or Zig implementation alternatives\nLLVM/MLIR service and external tools independently selected\nProvider version, ownership, ABI and object qualification"
matrix: "MG01-MG12 acceptance matrix\nNJS directly advances ownership and diagnostics by design\nEnables some FFI/provider/invalidation work\nDoes not install a GC, memory model or scheduler"
economics: "Separate language adoption gate\nRS01-RS12 residual code after Scheme/C-library/Zig reuse\nCA01-CA08 disjoint fixed/local/per-job/change costs\nPositive net bound required; modernity is not proof of Zig ROI" {
  style.fill: "#fff0ce"
}
goal -> semantic
goal -> runtime
semantic -> njs
runtime -> njs: "explicit gateway obligations"
njs -> providers
semantic -> matrix
runtime -> matrix
providers -> matrix
matrix -> economics
